00:08:57,538 --> 00:08:59,740
- Margie, wake up.

254
00:08:59,773 --> 00:09:01,475
Hurry now.

255
00:09:01,508 --> 00:09:03,777
JOEL:
They are youth in Asia.

256
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:04,978
TOM SERVO:
I don't believe you said that!

257
00:09:05,012 --> 00:09:07,013
- Well, do as you want.

258
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:10,217
- I'm the mischievous one.

259
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:14,188
- Stop watching TV
and brush your teeth.

260
00:09:14,222 --> 00:09:16,623
And do it properly
this morning, you hear?

261
00:09:16,657 --> 00:09:18,192
JOEL:
No more fish paste and sea weed,

262
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:19,860
please, Mom.

263
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:23,097
- Don't you want to have
nice shiny white teeth?

264
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:26,267
The Sea World animals
do it a lot better than you.

265
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,268
- Huh?

266
00:09:27,302 --> 00:09:29,403
- These Sea World whales
were brought here

267
00:09:29,437 --> 00:09:31,405
all the way from Canada
last year.

268
00:09:31,438 --> 00:09:32,607
- Uh-hm, uh-hm, uh-hm.

269
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,808
- ...is 10 months old.

270
00:09:34,842 --> 00:09:37,945
The other one, Chippie,
is a female.

271
00:09:37,978 --> 00:09:40,580
- Hurry, or you're going to be
late for school again.

272
00:09:40,615 --> 00:09:41,582
- Oh!

273
00:09:41,615 --> 00:09:43,517
- Oh, look at you.

274
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:45,118
Will you wash
that whipped cream off.

275
00:09:45,152 --> 00:09:47,888
Even the killer whales
rinse their mouths.

276
00:09:47,922 --> 00:09:49,790
- Killer whales spit take.

277
00:09:49,823 --> 00:09:51,792
[LAUGHTER]

278
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:53,393
- Are his teeth
in good condition.

279
00:09:53,427 --> 00:09:54,395
Would you take a look?

280
00:09:54,428 --> 00:09:56,163
- Sure.

281
00:09:56,197 --> 00:09:59,467
- [indistinct] the killer
whales here at Sea World and...

282
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,802
- Okay, bite down.

283
00:10:00,835 --> 00:10:01,968
- Oooh.

284
00:10:02,002 --> 00:10:04,772
- You know you must take
good care of your teeth

285
00:10:04,805 --> 00:10:06,640
or the dolphins
will make fun of you.

286
00:10:06,673 --> 00:10:07,875
- And Daddy won't love you.

287
00:10:07,908 --> 00:10:08,908
- Uh-hm.

288
00:10:10,077 --> 00:10:11,845
- Margie, Helen.

289
00:10:11,878 --> 00:10:14,415
You forgot something, wait.

290
00:10:14,448 --> 00:10:16,483
Your mother's
in a hospital in New York...

291
00:10:16,517 --> 00:10:17,585
- Detoxing.

292
00:10:17,618 --> 00:10:20,087
-...and you both forgot
to kiss her good-bye.

293
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,623
Go on, send your mother
a big kiss.

294
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:26,260
- Uh, so when do you
get off work anyway.

295
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:27,662
Uh-ha-uh-ha.

296
00:10:27,695 --> 00:10:30,832
[PANTING]

297
00:10:30,865 --> 00:10:32,800
- ...and say good-bye
to everyone now.

298
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:34,635
Have a nice rest.
We want you to...

299
00:10:34,668 --> 00:10:35,903
- Hey, they're
getting' hammered.

300
00:10:35,937 --> 00:10:37,003
What's goin' on?

301
00:10:37,037 --> 00:10:39,640
- ...next show at 2 o'clock
this afternoon.

302
00:10:39,673 --> 00:10:41,908
Good-bye now.

303
00:10:41,942 --> 00:10:43,877
- Bye.

304
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:44,945
- Good morning, Kenny.

305
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:46,647
- Good morning, Margie,
Good morning, Helen.

306
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,782
JOEL: Where's your hat?
- How's it going?

307
00:10:47,815 --> 00:10:48,882
- Never a dull moment.

308
00:10:48,915 --> 00:10:51,052
[LAUGHTER]

309
00:10:51,085 --> 00:10:52,753
- ...in the jungle
and have adventure...

310
00:10:52,787 --> 00:10:54,288
JOEL:
Just like the Goonies.

311
00:10:54,322 --> 00:10:56,290
- Now you two be good
and do everything

312
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:57,725
the teacher tells you,

313
00:10:57,758 --> 00:10:59,560
and you'll be
clever little children.

314
00:10:59,593 --> 00:11:01,362
As clever as the dolphins.

315
00:11:01,395 --> 00:11:04,365
- Stop, I hear that all
the time from my own parents.

316
00:11:04,398 --> 00:11:06,167
- If you want me
to be like a dolphin,

317
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,168
I'll have to learn
to swim first.

318
00:11:08,202 --> 00:11:09,170
- You'll have to learn
to blow air

319
00:11:09,203 --> 00:11:10,170
out of the back
of your neck too.

320
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:12,973
- ...and now for some
morning exercises.

321
00:11:13,007 --> 00:11:15,475
Jumbo is showing off
standing on his head.

322
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,477
- Jumbo?

323
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:17,945
- ...while
Sabu does a handstand.

324
00:11:17,978 --> 00:11:20,280
Now you mustn't
applaud yourself...

325
00:11:20,313 --> 00:11:23,683
[LAUGHTER]

326
00:11:23,717 --> 00:11:26,753
...would rather see
how well you play basketball.

327
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:29,823
I heard that you're
a regular champion.

328
00:11:29,857 --> 00:11:33,360
Noro has the ball and he's
going to try to score a point.

329
00:11:33,393 --> 00:11:34,528
Will he succeed?

330
00:11:34,562 --> 00:11:35,528
TOM SERVO:
Nice hat.

331
00:11:35,562 --> 00:11:36,697
- Bravo.

332
00:11:36,730 --> 00:11:39,467
How about giving him a hand,
ladies and gentlemen?

333
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,668
That's Noco,
our older lady seal,

334
00:11:41,702 --> 00:11:44,105
proving diving
isn't just a male sport.

335
00:11:44,138 --> 00:11:45,372
Good girl!

336
00:11:45,405 --> 00:11:47,875
And now, a swimming race.

337
00:11:47,908 --> 00:11:49,577
A real Olympic contest.

338
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:51,112
JOEL:
Aw, all the Canadian seals

339
00:11:51,145 --> 00:11:52,680
are on steroids.

340
00:11:52,713 --> 00:11:53,947
- ...seems to be gaining.

341
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:56,817
No, it's Noro followed
by Sabu and Noco,

342
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:59,653
and Noro wins,
so Noro gets the gold medal.

343
00:11:59,687 --> 00:12:01,888
- Uh-oh. He gives
the black power salute

344
00:12:01,922 --> 00:12:03,023
and is stripped of his medal.

345
00:12:03,057 --> 00:12:04,458
- and our charming Noco
gets the bronze

346
00:12:04,492 --> 00:12:06,427
and peanuts for the others.

347
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:07,595
- Peanuts?

348
00:12:07,628 --> 00:12:09,097
- Oh, and that's their reward?

349
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:11,065
Getting stuffed?

350
00:12:11,098 --> 00:12:14,502
- Do you mean
that you have to dissect her

351
00:12:14,535 --> 00:12:16,237
to find out why she died?

352
00:12:16,270 --> 00:12:17,505
- That's right.

353
00:12:17,538 --> 00:12:19,440
We have to discover
what caused her death

354
00:12:19,473 --> 00:12:20,740
to protect
the other animals.

355
00:12:20,775 --> 00:12:22,810
- Then she goes up
on my office wall.

356
00:12:22,843 --> 00:12:25,545
- Mr. Yamoto,
we know you treated them

357
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:27,047
exactly like your children,

358
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,782
so we understand
how you feel.

359
00:12:28,815 --> 00:12:29,883
- Indifferent?

360
00:12:29,917 --> 00:12:32,418
[LAUGHS]

361
00:12:32,453 --> 00:12:35,455
[♪♪♪]

362
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:41,095
- Kathryn...

363
00:12:42,730 --> 00:12:43,830
have you seen Helen?

364
00:12:43,863 --> 00:12:45,332
She hasn't come back yet.

365
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:47,768
- No, she was playing
with Kenny awhile ago.

366
00:12:47,802 --> 00:12:49,703
- Honey, time for a new apron.

367
00:12:49,737 --> 00:12:51,172
- Uh-hm.

368
00:12:51,205 --> 00:12:52,573
- They left their things here.

369
00:12:52,607 --> 00:12:54,040
- And they didn't
separate their colors.

370
00:12:54,073 --> 00:12:55,943
- Things appear
and disappear like magic.

371
00:12:55,977 --> 00:12:57,143
- They sure do!

372
00:12:57,177 --> 00:12:59,180
[LAUGHTER]

373
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,583
- Oh, Heathcliff.

374
00:13:06,487 --> 00:13:07,488
- Wuthering Heights.

375
00:13:08,855 --> 00:13:09,890
- Babe Winkelman.

376
00:13:09,923 --> 00:13:10,892
- Hm.

377
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,125
- If things go on like this,

378
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:14,093
the whole coastline
will be polluted.

379
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:16,230
- Yeah, nothing
can live in this.

380
00:13:16,263 --> 00:13:18,432
There won't be a fish left
in a few years.

381
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:20,902
- Maybe dolphins.
- ...it would be our own fault.

382
00:13:20,935 --> 00:13:23,403
- Science always
seem to destroy nature

383
00:13:23,437 --> 00:13:25,840
instead of doing
everything to protect it.

384
00:13:25,873 --> 00:13:28,542
It's up to biologists like us
to warn the world

385
00:13:28,575 --> 00:13:30,043
what's happening around us.

386
00:13:30,077 --> 00:13:32,145
- Yeah, save the message
for the end of the movie.

387
00:13:32,178 --> 00:13:34,382
- We bring you a special news
announcement.

388
00:13:34,415 --> 00:13:36,050
A special news announcement.

389
00:13:36,083 --> 00:13:37,350
At 9 AM today,

390
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:39,887
there was a major earthquake
in the Indian Ocean.

391
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,622
- Hm.
- Ten thousand people died

392
00:13:41,655 --> 00:13:43,923
and hundreds of thousands
were injured.

393
00:13:43,957 --> 00:13:45,025
The force of the earthquake

394
00:13:45,058 --> 00:13:47,360
was one of the greatest
ever recorded.

395
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:49,128
Magnitude 16...

396
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:50,630
- I'm going to the top
of the [indistinct].

397
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,900
- ...more powerful than the one
that rocked Peru yesterday.

398
00:13:52,933 --> 00:13:55,535
I repeat, today at 9 AM,
there was...

399
00:13:55,568 --> 00:13:58,205
- One earthquake
right after the other.

400
00:13:58,238 --> 00:13:59,207
It's awful.

401
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,207
- Did you hear?

402
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,342
A force of magnitude 16 is,

403
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:03,810
and on opposite sides
of the earth.

404
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:04,812
- Hm.

405
00:14:04,845 --> 00:14:06,180
- Incredible, isn't it?

406
00:14:06,213 --> 00:14:07,180
- Very strange.

407
00:14:07,213 --> 00:14:08,482
- No more than
those stretch pants.

408
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:09,617
- Time for a little snack.

409
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:10,885
- Okay.
- Uh-hm.

410
00:14:10,918 --> 00:14:13,420
- Kathryn prepared one of her
specialties, lemonade...

411
00:14:13,453 --> 00:14:14,955
- ...and I've got your
sister's specialty,

412
00:14:14,988 --> 00:14:16,257
peanut butter sandwiches.

413
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:17,323
- Hey, hey...

414
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:19,025
- You leave my sister
out of this. Shut up.

415
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:21,595
Take it back, take it back,
you rotten, crummy...

416
00:14:23,463 --> 00:14:24,432
- Uh-oh.

417
00:14:24,465 --> 00:14:26,200
- Hey, my jigger of gin
is empty.

418
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:27,367
- My sister forgot
the sandwiches.

419
00:14:29,437 --> 00:14:34,207
- Naw, I saw her put them in.

420
00:14:34,242 --> 00:14:36,043
- And I saw Kathryn fill this.

421
00:14:36,077 --> 00:14:37,043
- What happened then?

422
00:14:37,077 --> 00:14:38,078
- Maybe your sister ate them.

423
00:14:38,112 --> 00:14:40,247
- Shut up about my sister,
shut up.

424
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:45,485
- [indistinct] pitchfork.
- Aha.

425
00:14:45,518 --> 00:14:46,820
- I don't feel well.

426
00:14:46,853 --> 00:14:48,355
I think I ate too much.

427
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,623
Have you got any medicine?

428
00:14:49,657 --> 00:14:51,425
- I want a Coke, Daddy.

429
00:14:51,458 --> 00:14:53,227
- Kenny, didn't I tell you

430
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:55,362
not to come here
without permission?

431
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:56,897
- Helen, when we get home,

432
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:58,265
you'll get a nice spanking.

433
00:14:58,298 --> 00:14:59,867
- Can I have it now?
- What's that?

434
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,135
What's that thing over there?

435
00:15:01,168 --> 00:15:04,203
- Kenny, now don't try to
change the subject.

436
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:06,907
- Look, look at that,
in the sky.

437
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,842
TOM SERVO:
See it? Um.

438
00:15:08,875 --> 00:15:10,945
JOEL:
Maybe they have sandwiches.

439
00:15:10,978 --> 00:15:12,112
- Strange looking.

440
00:15:12,145 --> 00:15:14,615
- It could be an artificial
satellite that's fallen.

441
00:15:14,648 --> 00:15:15,615
JOEL:
Maybe it's a HoJos.

442
00:15:15,648 --> 00:15:18,418
- ...or else
a kind of space station.

443
00:15:18,452 --> 00:15:19,653
- Well, whatever it is,

444
00:15:19,687 --> 00:15:21,588
we can't afford to
show it [indistinct].

445
00:15:21,622 --> 00:15:23,423
- Meanwhile, at Dollyworld...

446
00:15:24,958 --> 00:15:26,927
- Outside is
an unidentified object.

447
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:29,497
It was first seen off the coast
of Kanagawa City.

448
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:30,830
- Five miles from Cucamonga.

449
00:15:30,863 --> 00:15:32,265
- ...[indistinct] to the sea.

450
00:15:32,298 --> 00:15:37,003
Latitude 34-40 NW,
longitude 140-20 SW.

451
00:15:37,037 --> 00:15:39,138
- Henry.
- Portrait of a serial killer.

452
00:15:39,172 --> 00:15:40,773
- You know the waters
are deep there,

453
00:15:40,807 --> 00:15:42,375
and it's the dolphin's
favorite spot.

454
00:15:42,408 --> 00:15:43,377
- Hm.

455
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:45,045
- It would be tragic
if they got hurt.

456
00:15:45,078 --> 00:15:46,180
- Tom, shall we look?

457
00:15:46,213 --> 00:15:47,547
- Sure.
- Hmm.

458
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:48,848
- But what about the kids?

459
00:15:48,882 --> 00:15:50,483
- I'll go too,
after all I am the son

460
00:15:50,517 --> 00:15:52,118
of a marine life biologist.

461
00:15:52,152 --> 00:15:53,520
- And I wanna go too, Daddy.

462
00:15:53,553 --> 00:15:55,122
- Okay, okay.
You collaborators.

463
00:15:55,155 --> 00:15:58,192
- Yeah, maybe they have
Coke out there, kid.

464
00:15:58,225 --> 00:16:00,760
- Hey, look,
it's Fredo Corleone. Huh.

465
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,663
Pitshu!

466
00:16:04,932 --> 00:16:07,735
ALL:
♪ Casper the friendly ghost ♪

467
00:16:07,768 --> 00:16:08,768
- Shhh!

468
00:16:13,473 --> 00:16:17,310
- And Little Audrey says...

469
00:16:18,712 --> 00:16:20,880
- This is terrific!

470
00:16:20,913 --> 00:16:23,450
- Hey, it's just a boat,
come on.

471
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:26,320
- Hey, look, Dots,
jelly beans, Skittles,

472
00:16:26,353 --> 00:16:29,557
Gummi Bears, Jujubes. Umm!

473
00:16:31,692 --> 00:16:32,693
- Piles!

474
00:16:35,095 --> 00:16:37,097
- Hey, who roached?

475
00:16:39,733 --> 00:16:42,535
- M&Ms, melt underwater,
not in your hand.

476
00:16:49,142 --> 00:16:50,443
- Uh?

477
00:16:50,477 --> 00:16:51,945
- Gamera!

478
00:16:51,978 --> 00:16:54,013
- Please welcome your host
and emcee

479
00:16:54,047 --> 00:16:57,752
from Monsterland in Miami Beach,
Gamera!

480
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,088
- Gamera's here!

481
00:17:02,122 --> 00:17:04,290
- I don't like monsters.

482
00:17:04,323 --> 00:17:06,560
- Gamera is the friend
of all children.

483
00:17:06,593 --> 00:17:07,795
- Is he, really?

484
00:17:07,828 --> 00:17:08,928
- Yeah,
if you get on his good side,

485
00:17:08,962 --> 00:17:10,897
but don't cross him.

486
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:14,133
[MONSTER ROARS]

487
00:17:14,167 --> 00:17:15,135
- You know what's weird,

488
00:17:15,168 --> 00:17:16,503
but even the monster's
badly dubbed.

489
00:17:16,537 --> 00:17:18,172
- Yeah.
- ...he answers.

490
00:17:18,205 --> 00:17:19,940
- Monsters can't talk.

491
00:17:19,973 --> 00:17:21,408
- You read too much!

492
00:17:22,977 --> 00:17:24,310
- Ha, ha, he's lapping them.

493
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:25,345
- Cool.

494
00:17:31,352 --> 00:17:32,452
- Uh-oh.

495
00:17:32,485 --> 00:17:34,087
- Hey, who runs
the flying saucer?

496
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:36,090
Timothy William?

497
00:17:36,123 --> 00:17:37,223
- Uh-oh, I'm outta here.

498
00:17:37,257 --> 00:17:38,292
I'm going home.

499
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:39,392
Uh-hm.

500
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:44,732
[MONSTER ROARS]

501
00:17:44,765 --> 00:17:46,333
- What, what?

502
00:17:48,268 --> 00:17:50,603
ZIGRA WOMAN:
I have obeyed your orders,
Zigra.

503
00:17:50,637 --> 00:17:52,940
I have brought
the earth creatures to you.

504
00:17:52,973 --> 00:17:55,008
ZIGRA:
Good work.

505
00:17:55,042 --> 00:17:56,410
I am pleased...

506
00:17:56,443 --> 00:17:57,443
- As punch.

507
00:17:57,477 --> 00:17:59,980
ZIGRA:
Now, awaken them.

508
00:18:00,013 --> 00:18:02,783
- Pay no attention to the man
behind the curtain.

509
00:18:02,817 --> 00:18:05,318
ZIGRA WOMAN:
Yes, Zigra. Creatures of
the earth, wake up!

510
00:18:05,352 --> 00:18:07,753
- You know, it looks
kind like the Hullabaloo set

511
00:18:07,788 --> 00:18:09,388
except for that monster.

512
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:10,990
