I want a cracker, a big one.

2234
01:17:15,598 --> 01:17:18,368
ZIGRA:
Surrender to me at once.

2235
01:17:18,402 --> 01:17:22,572
It's very easy for me
to destroy the Bathyscope.

2236
01:17:22,605 --> 01:17:24,373
CROW:
Must not be built Ford tough.

2237
01:17:24,407 --> 01:17:27,110
ZIGRA:
If you surrender
within an hour,

2238
01:17:27,143 --> 01:17:29,245
I promise you
I will save you.

2239
01:17:29,278 --> 01:17:31,582
TOM SERVO:
It would be like
surrendering to Kukla.

2240
01:17:31,615 --> 01:17:33,483
JOEL: Yeah.
CROW: In his palace.

2241
01:17:33,517 --> 01:17:35,318
ZIGRA:
If you do not surrender,

2242
01:17:35,352 --> 01:17:38,222
I will destroy the Bathyscope

2243
01:17:38,255 --> 01:17:41,625
and your friends
inside will die.

2244
01:17:41,658 --> 01:17:43,260
CROW:
Well, that kinda follows,
doesn't it?

2245
01:17:43,293 --> 01:17:44,260
ZIGRA:
This is my last warning.

2246
01:17:44,293 --> 01:17:46,430
I am losing my patience.

2247
01:17:46,463 --> 01:17:49,365
Zigra is your master now.

2248
01:17:49,398 --> 01:17:50,533
JOEL:
Hey, you're a fish.

2249
01:17:50,567 --> 01:17:54,337
ZIGRA:
And you will obey me
from now on.

2250
01:17:54,370 --> 01:17:55,605
CROW:
They're watching TNT,

2251
01:17:55,638 --> 01:17:58,042
one of our favorite networks.

2252
01:17:58,075 --> 01:18:00,777
- Zigra is a deep-sea monster,

2253
01:18:00,810 --> 01:18:03,180
and he loves to feed
on human beings.

2254
01:18:03,213 --> 01:18:05,582
JOEL:
Yeah, we figured that out,
thanks.

2255
01:18:05,615 --> 01:18:07,117
- And after
we surrender to Zigra,

2256
01:18:07,150 --> 01:18:09,285
he'll imprison us
in cages like animals

2257
01:18:09,318 --> 01:18:11,153
and keep us all
for his food.

2258
01:18:12,755 --> 01:18:14,557
- How's your supply of oxygen?

2259
01:18:14,590 --> 01:18:16,893
- Enough for about 60 minutes.

2260
01:18:16,927 --> 01:18:18,095
- Oh Papa!
TOM SERVO: Wait, wait.

2261
01:18:18,128 --> 01:18:21,330
I found some more oxygen
in a drawer, we're Okay.

2262
01:18:21,363 --> 01:18:23,167
- We'll surrender
to Zigra at once.

2263
01:18:23,200 --> 01:18:25,102
- Oh [indistinct] no.

2264
01:18:25,135 --> 01:18:26,202
JOEL:
Wait a minute!

2265
01:18:26,235 --> 01:18:27,203
CROW:
There's more...

2266
01:18:27,237 --> 01:18:28,572
- Bathyscope, you hear me.

2267
01:18:28,605 --> 01:18:31,207
We're not
going to let you die.

2268
01:18:31,240 --> 01:18:32,842
Sergeant,
call UN Headquarters.

2269
01:18:32,875 --> 01:18:33,843
- Right.

2270
01:18:33,877 --> 01:18:34,945
TOM SERVO:
This is a pickle, George.

2271
01:18:34,978 --> 01:18:36,345
This is a pickle.

2272
01:18:36,378 --> 01:18:38,782
- Zigra, do you hear me?

2273
01:18:38,815 --> 01:18:41,050
I admit,
you're more powerful

2274
01:18:41,083 --> 01:18:42,918
and advanced in science
than we are.

2275
01:18:42,952 --> 01:18:44,220
CROW:
Go on, I'm listening.

2276
01:18:44,253 --> 01:18:45,455
- We cannot defeat you.

2277
01:18:45,488 --> 01:18:46,457
Our weapons are too weak.

2278
01:18:46,490 --> 01:18:47,857
CROW:
Now tell me I'm pretty...

2279
01:18:47,890 --> 01:18:49,492
- We want only one thing...

2280
01:18:49,525 --> 01:18:51,562
the Bathyscope to be saved.

2281
01:18:51,595 --> 01:18:53,197
We surrender to you at once.

2282
01:18:53,230 --> 01:18:54,965
JOEL and ROBOTS:
Say please.

2283
01:18:54,998 --> 01:18:56,398
- Very well.

2284
01:18:56,433 --> 01:18:58,968
Turn off the light
in the Bathyscope.

2285
01:18:59,002 --> 01:19:01,337
CROW:
And give someone else
a turn in there.

2286
01:19:02,872 --> 01:19:05,042
JOEL:
You know, he's got
Lillian Hellman eyes.

2287
01:19:05,075 --> 01:19:06,677
CROW:
He does.

2288
01:19:06,710 --> 01:19:08,112
- We're saved now.

2289
01:19:08,145 --> 01:19:09,145
TOM SERVO:
Have you been saved?

2290
01:19:09,178 --> 01:19:10,280
- Is that right, Papa?

2291
01:19:10,313 --> 01:19:11,313
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2292
01:19:15,685 --> 01:19:17,587
TOM SERVO:
Uh, oh.

2293
01:19:17,620 --> 01:19:19,622
ZIGRA WOMAN:
You know even if you surrender,

2294
01:19:19,655 --> 01:19:21,958
mankind will become its food.

2295
01:19:21,992 --> 01:19:25,062
You mustn't trust Zigra.

2296
01:19:25,095 --> 01:19:27,163
Dr. Henry, listen.

2297
01:19:27,197 --> 01:19:30,400
You are an authority
on marine life, the greatest...

2298
01:19:30,433 --> 01:19:31,635
CROW:
Well, I do my best, over.

2299
01:19:31,668 --> 01:19:33,370
- ...Zigra's main
characteristic.

2300
01:19:33,403 --> 01:19:35,905
If you remember that,
you'll have a great weapon.

2301
01:19:35,938 --> 01:19:38,375
It's your only chance
to escape Zigra.

2302
01:19:38,408 --> 01:19:42,645
It's your only chance,
so you must try it.

2303
01:19:42,678 --> 01:19:45,015
- Zigra's main characteristic?

2304
01:19:45,048 --> 01:19:46,983
Of course, he's French.

2305
01:19:47,017 --> 01:19:49,418
TOM SERVO:
He's not French, he's Belgian.

2306
01:19:49,452 --> 01:19:51,488
- And this time, stay there.

2307
01:19:51,522 --> 01:19:54,390
Up you go and don't move.

2308
01:19:54,423 --> 01:19:55,458
- Okay now.

2309
01:19:55,492 --> 01:19:58,228
- Go on, go.

2310
01:19:58,262 --> 01:19:59,262
CROW:
I'll bet.

2311
01:20:02,398 --> 01:20:03,933
- Raise the voltage.

2312
01:20:03,967 --> 01:20:04,935
TOM SERVO:
Damn it, darn it.

2313
01:20:04,968 --> 01:20:06,770
You got your
high beams on, dude.

2314
01:20:14,377 --> 01:20:16,345
- Oh, it's working.
I knew it.

2315
01:20:16,378 --> 01:20:17,647
CROW:
Now we can project movies
on him.

2316
01:20:19,515 --> 01:20:22,618
JOEL:
Spotlight dance on Zigra.

2317
01:20:22,652 --> 01:20:24,420
TOM SERVO:
Full reverse, full reverse.

2318
01:20:37,067 --> 01:20:39,302
- This is counter-defense
headquarters, come in.

2319
01:20:39,335 --> 01:20:40,937
CROW:
This is counterproductive here.

2320
01:20:40,970 --> 01:20:41,938
- Please answer.

2321
01:20:41,972 --> 01:20:44,473
- Dr. Henry,
Mr. Wallace, please answer.

2322
01:20:44,507 --> 01:20:45,475
Please answer.

2323
01:20:45,508 --> 01:20:48,645
TOM SERVO:
I'm trying, I'm trying.

2324
01:20:48,678 --> 01:20:50,580
- Dr. Henry, Mr. Wallace.

2325
01:20:50,613 --> 01:20:53,250
Come in, come in.

2326
01:20:53,283 --> 01:20:54,350
Answer please.

2327
01:20:54,383 --> 01:20:55,852
Answer please.

2328
01:20:55,885 --> 01:20:57,153
- Answer!

2329
01:20:57,187 --> 01:20:58,153
Henry!

2330
01:20:58,187 --> 01:21:00,423
- Papa! Come in, Papa!

2331
01:21:00,457 --> 01:21:01,725
JOEL:
Go to the door and answer

2332
01:21:01,758 --> 01:21:03,660
in the form of a question.

2333
01:21:03,693 --> 01:21:06,295
- All this is entirely my fault.

2334
01:21:06,328 --> 01:21:08,732
I shouldn't
have given that message.

2335
01:21:08,765 --> 01:21:09,698
CROW:
She's right. It's her fault.

2336
01:21:09,732 --> 01:21:10,767
Let's get her.

2337
01:21:10,800 --> 01:21:12,902
- We'll all be eaten
by Zigra sooner or later.

2338
01:21:15,038 --> 01:21:17,040
JOEL:
Hey, this isn't really that sad.

2339
01:21:17,073 --> 01:21:19,642
[THUNDER AND LIGHTNING]

2340
01:21:19,675 --> 01:21:22,212
CROW:
Penitentiary Three.

2341
01:21:22,245 --> 01:21:24,447
TOM SERVO:
It was a dark and stormy night.

2342
01:21:32,988 --> 01:21:35,258
CROW:
Whoa, Gamera.
You're on the air.

2343
01:21:35,292 --> 01:21:37,227
TOM SERVO:
Oh my gosh, I overslept.

2344
01:21:37,260 --> 01:21:38,862
I'm gonna miss the bus.

2345
01:21:44,533 --> 01:21:48,237
JOEL:
Hawaii Five-0?

2346
01:21:48,272 --> 01:21:49,705
Oh.

2347
01:21:49,738 --> 01:21:51,140
CROW:
Oh Moon Doggie,

2348
01:21:51,173 --> 01:21:54,677
let's get married, Frankie.

2349
01:21:54,710 --> 01:21:55,712
JOEL:
I know. It's almost over.

2350
01:21:55,745 --> 01:21:57,880
Just hang in there, folks,
come on.

2351
01:22:01,117 --> 01:22:03,152
TOM SERVO:
You see, itching, flaking...

2352
01:22:03,185 --> 01:22:04,387
I think it's dandruff.

2353
01:22:05,822 --> 01:22:06,990
CROW:
Hm.

2354
01:22:07,023 --> 01:22:12,428
TOM SERVO:
♪ Why am I alone
With my dark star? ♪

2355
01:22:12,462 --> 01:22:13,930
- Uh, Gamera's gone.

2356
01:22:13,963 --> 01:22:14,930
- What?

2357
01:22:14,965 --> 01:22:15,965
CROW:
[indistinct] got 'em.

2358
01:22:19,435 --> 01:22:22,605
- Do you think Gamera
will try to save the Bathyscope?

2359
01:22:22,638 --> 01:22:24,840
- Even if he does try,

2360
01:22:24,873 --> 01:22:26,810
the oxygen supply
in the Bathyscope

2361
01:22:26,843 --> 01:22:29,245
must have given out
over eight hours ago.

2362
01:22:29,278 --> 01:22:30,413
CROW:
Yep.

2363
01:22:30,447 --> 01:22:33,048
JOEL:
Mommy, make that guy
stop looking at me.

2364
01:22:33,082 --> 01:22:35,385
CROW: Heh, heh, heh.
- And he died of suffocation.

2365
01:22:35,418 --> 01:22:36,385
TOM SERVO:
Did I get that right,

2366
01:22:36,418 --> 01:22:38,388
they died on vacation? Hm.

2367
01:22:38,422 --> 01:22:39,522
CROW:
Aw, who cares?

2368
01:22:39,555 --> 01:22:40,523
Come on.

2369
01:22:40,557 --> 01:22:43,158
[♪♪♪]

2370
01:22:46,963 --> 01:22:49,898
- Save them, Gamera,
save them!

2371
01:22:49,932 --> 01:22:50,867
- Stay back.

2372
01:22:50,900 --> 01:22:51,968
Don't get too close.

2373
01:22:52,002 --> 01:22:53,068
JOEL:
Look, I'm not gonna get this

2374
01:22:53,102 --> 01:22:54,070
out of the gutter

2375
01:22:54,103 --> 01:22:56,272
every time you kids
throw it up there. Okay?

2376
01:22:57,740 --> 01:22:58,708
CROW:
Now don't call me

2377
01:22:58,742 --> 01:23:00,110
unless you really need me.

2378
01:23:02,712 --> 01:23:04,380
Right?

2379
01:23:04,413 --> 01:23:06,082
- All right.
Let's get them.

2380
01:23:07,950 --> 01:23:09,618
CROW:
Uh, did we miss something?

2381
01:23:09,652 --> 01:23:12,188
TOM SERVO:
Uh, is this underwater?

2382
01:23:12,222 --> 01:23:13,390
JOEL:
I think.

2383
01:23:13,423 --> 01:23:14,390
- Get the stretcher.

2384
01:23:14,423 --> 01:23:15,392
Gently, gently!

2385
01:23:15,425 --> 01:23:16,860
JOEL:
Looks like a big port-a-potty.

2386
01:23:16,893 --> 01:23:19,128
TOM SERVO:
Um. We did miss something.

2387
01:23:28,538 --> 01:23:30,507
- Henry, Henry!

2388
01:23:30,540 --> 01:23:32,242
- Papa, Papa!

2389
01:23:32,275 --> 01:23:33,242
JOEL:
Is there an echo?

2390
01:23:33,275 --> 01:23:35,245
- Put them down over here.

2391
01:23:35,278 --> 01:23:36,980
CROW:
Put 'em down.
Okay, they're ugly.

2392
01:23:37,013 --> 01:23:38,815
Ha, ha.

2393
01:23:38,848 --> 01:23:40,250
- Kenny!
- Helen!

2394
01:23:40,283 --> 01:23:42,718
TOM SERVO:
George, Heathcliff, McCloud.

2395
01:23:42,752 --> 01:23:45,055
- Did they die of suffocation?

2396
01:23:45,088 --> 01:23:46,688
- They're dead,
but not by suffocation.

2397
01:23:46,723 --> 01:23:47,690
CROW:
Oh that's a relief.

2398
01:23:47,723 --> 01:23:48,758
JOEL and TOM SERVO:
Huh?

2399
01:23:48,792 --> 01:23:50,060
- I think I know.

2400
01:23:50,093 --> 01:23:52,595
The ray has stopped
cellular activity,

2401
01:23:52,628 --> 01:23:54,663
so now all the cells
are dormant.

2402
01:23:54,697 --> 01:23:57,033
- Then, then
they're not... dead.

2403
01:23:57,067 --> 01:23:58,768
JOEL:
No, but they might as well be.

2404
01:23:58,802 --> 01:24:00,403
- There's a very good hope
of reviving them.

2405
01:24:00,437 --> 01:24:01,403
- Oh!

2406
01:24:01,437 --> 01:24:02,972
- Zigra was angered
by what Lora Lee said,

2407
01:24:03,005 --> 01:24:04,040
so it sent out its ray...

2408
01:24:04,073 --> 01:24:05,040
TOM SERVO:
Huh.

2409
01:24:05,075 --> 01:24:06,142
- ...which suspended
organic activity,

2410
01:24:06,175 --> 01:24:08,010
and that's the reason
they're not dead.

2411
01:24:08,043 --> 01:24:09,545
- Yes, exactly.

2412
01:24:09,578 --> 01:24:10,547
TOM SERVO:
So it's a man ray.

2413
01:24:10,580 --> 01:24:12,915
- If they had suffocated
from lack of oxygen,

2414
01:24:12,948 --> 01:24:15,752
there wouldn't be any way
of reviving them.

2415
01:24:15,785 --> 01:24:17,887
JOEL:
So they're only mostly dead.

2416
01:24:17,920 --> 01:24:19,288
ZIGRA WOMAN:
No, don't thank me yet.

2417
01:24:19,322 --> 01:24:21,423
Thank me
after they've recovered.

2418
01:24:21,457 --> 01:24:23,593
- Doctor,
how will you treat them?

2419
01:24:23,627 --> 01:24:24,593
TOM SERVO:
Incompetently.

2420
01:24:24,627 --> 01:24:25,795
- Electric shocks.

2421
01:24:25,828 --> 01:24:26,963
Gamera, don't forget,

2422
01:24:26,997 --> 01:24:29,365
was also revived by a series
of light beam shocks.

2423
01:24:29,398 --> 01:24:30,967
- That's true.

2424
01:24:31,000 --> 01:24:33,335
Sergeant, make preparations
to revive them.

2425
01:24:33,368 --> 01:24:35,205
CROW:
And get those cattle
prods out of my trunk...

2426
01:24:39,742 --> 01:24:42,445
Oh, I dreamed I ate
[indistinct],

2427
01:24:42,478 --> 01:24:43,613
and I'm not [indistinct].

2428
01:24:43,647 --> 01:24:44,613
Go figure.

2429
01:24:44,647 --> 01:24:47,717
[MONSTER ROARS]

2430
01:24:47,750 --> 01:24:50,120
JOEL:
You know, I see
a monster fight coming on;

2431
01:24:50,153 --> 01:24:53,388
I can't tell why,
but I just do.

2432
01:24:53,422 --> 01:24:54,390
CROW:
Well, look at him.

2433
01:24:54,423 --> 01:24:56,125
He looks like
a stealth sturgeon.

2434
01:24:56,158 --> 01:24:58,928
[MONSTER ROARS]

2435
01:25:02,832 --> 01:25:04,133
CROW:
Come on, come on.

2436
01:25:04,167 --> 01:25:05,302
Pick me up.

2437
01:25:05,335 --> 01:25:07,070
[MONSTER ROARS]

2438
01:25:07,103 --> 01:25:08,938
TOM SERVO:
I'm not the one
that wants to break up.

2439
01:25:08,972 --> 01:25:09,938
CROW:
Yeah, yeah.

2440
01:25:09,972 --> 01:25:11,573
Well,
I'm keeping all your albums.

2441
01:25:11,607 --> 01:25:12,575
TOM SERVO:
Is this your copy

2442
01:25:12,608 --> 01:25:13,643
of "Catcher in the Rye"?

2443
01:25:13,677 --> 01:25:15,578
CROW:
Come on, give it back to me,
come on.

2444
01:25:15,612 --> 01:25:17,180
Nah, keep it.
What do I care?

2445
01:25:18,515 --> 01:25:20,115
[MONSTER ROARS]

2446
01:25:20,150 --> 01:25:21,617
JOEL:
Plenty of room, come on.

2447
01:25:21,650 --> 01:25:24,820
Bring it in.
Come on.

2448
01:25:24,853 --> 01:25:25,922
TOM SERVO:
Oo-o-h.

2449
01:25:25,955 --> 01:25:27,257
Dishwashing liquid.

2450
01:25:27,290 --> 01:25:28,892
CROW:
Gamera's soaking in it.

2451
01:25:30,627 --> 01:25:33,863
[MONSTER ROARS]

2452
01:25:37,300 --> 01:25:38,968
JOEL:
Nice lines on that monster,
though.

2453
01:25:39,002 --> 01:25:39,968
CROW:
All right.
Look at this one.

2454
01:25:40,002 --> 01:25:41,170
How about that?
Can you do that?

2455
01:25:41,203 --> 01:25:43,205
JOEL:
[indistinct].

2456
01:25:47,310 --> 01:25:49,312
You know, Gamera's
never seen the [indistinct].

2457
01:25:49,345 --> 01:25:50,413
CROW:
Ah, it shows.

2458
01:25:50,447 --> 01:25:51,780
JOEL:
Uh-hm.

2459
01:25:51,813 --> 01:25:52,782
CROW:
Gentile.

2460
01:25:52,815 --> 01:25:54,083
[LAUGHS]

2461
01:25:57,353 --> 01:25:59,155
CROW:
Look, he's on stand-up suit now.

2462
01:25:59,188 --> 01:26:02,425
JOEL:
No, I just had my teeth x-rayed,
come on.

2463
01:26:02,458 --> 01:26:04,393
TOM SERVO:
Ha, he had jalapenos for lunch.

2464
01:26:04,427 --> 01:26:06,395
JOEL:
I guess so.

2465
01:26:06,428 --> 01:26:07,430
CROW:
Ooops.

2466
01:26:09,298 --> 01:26:12,035
TOM SERVO:
Whoa, he can't take it there.

2467
01:26:12,068 --> 01:26:13,837
They can't take it there.

2468
01:26:15,638 --> 01:26:16,638
CROW:
Ooops.

2469
01:26:20,410 --> 01:26:22,745
TOM SERVO:
Ouch. Zorro, the gay blade.

2470
01:26:24,347 --> 01:26:26,682
JOEL:
Hey, Gamera's got stigmata...

2471
01:26:29,685 --> 01:26:32,222
oh, I hope
he's not playing hangman.

2472
01:26:32,255 --> 01:26:33,422
TOM SERVO:
We could be here a while.

2473
01:26:33,455 --> 01:26:34,623
CROW:
Tic-tac-toe.

2474
01:26:36,425 --> 01:26:37,527
TOM SERVO:
Whoo-hoo, oops.

2475
